 "transcript": {
  "answer": "No, the Aussie is strong against the yen right now. The yen is the weaker currency.\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 bought about **¥109.67** on 16 October 2026, the most recent RBA daily figure.\n- **Recent peak:** About **¥114.5** in August 2026. It has since eased by roughly 4%.\n- **A year ago:** About **¥100.8** at end-October 2025, so the Aussie is up roughly 9% against the yen over the year.\n- **Longer view:** At the start of 2024 it was about ¥97, and in April 2025 it fell to about ¥91.4. The current rate is well above both.\n\nThe Aussie has recently been trading near its strongest level against the yen in the past few years.",
